{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization fits this workflow without weakening coverage or adding disallowed access. The workflow is a GitHub Pages deployment pipeline (push to main plus workflow_dispatch), not a test/build matrix, so test selection, prioritization, fail-fast, and schedule-based patterns (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST, P-LIT-SELECT, P-LIT-PRIORITIZE, P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE, P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE) do not apply. P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW is not supported because no repository skip policy is evidenced and omitting a deploy changes required-check/deployment semantics. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE does not clearly apply: the mise-action step already enables caching (cache: true) for the toolchain, and there is no separate lockfile-governed dependency install (e.g., npm/go/pip) to key an additional actions/cache on; adding a redundant cache would be an unrelated change. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is already partially addressed by the existing concurrency group with cancel-in-progress: true; canceling queued/superseded runs would require GitHub API calls, adding network access and a privileged token, which is disallowed. No unused outputs, representative duration history for a custom timeout, or matrix to cancel were identified.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-SKIP-WORKFLOW", "P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE"]
}
